  "_key": "!scenes!b52232ce011e8f6e",
  "description": "<p>The runners arrive by night; the building looks deserted, no lights, nothing moving — except perhaps something on the roof.</p><p><strong>Two sentries</strong> are outside, both Flesh Form Soldiers (F3). The Queen is not yet fully summoned, so there is no true hive-mind yet: they can be killed <em>without</em> alerting the Hive, but given the chance they run for the building. Inside among the machinery, two Flesh Form Workers (F1) flee downstairs to warn Craft if they spot intruders.</p><p>The doors in the building's walls lead onto <strong>The Hive — Main Level</strong>; the roof access leads down its stairway.</p><p><strong>Rooms:</strong> The Amber Gel compound at night: the fenced lot, grass and pavement, the building's roof with its roof access, and the gates.</p><p><em>Layout derived from the printed floorplan on Queen Euphoria p.43. Measured 40 × 35 m by legend square = 2 m; 1 m = 24.2 px on a 300 dpi render of p.43 (PDF 45). The compound is 20 x 17.5 printed squares; the building inside it measures 24 x 8 m plus the 8 x 4 m wing, matching the Main Level plan exactly — the map carries a \"□ = 1 metre\" legend, so the scale is the book's, not an estimate.</em></p>"
}
